error_signature: "This header is only meant to be used on x86 and x64 architecture"
root_cause: "Vendored C sources include x86-only SIMD headers (<emmintrin.h>/<xmmintrin.h>/<mmintrin.h>) unconditionally, so on aarch64 (OHOS/HarmonyOS PC) the compiler stops with 'This header is only meant to be used on x86 and x64 architecture' before any source error appears. Here ksw.c (fermi-lite 0.1 bundled klib ksw, 2011 Attractive Chaos code) has no portable fallback at all: the whole alignment kernel is SSE2-only."
rec_approach: "Gate the x86 SIMD code behind `#if defined(__SSE2__)` and provide portable scalar implementations of the same kernel for the `#else` branch (ksw_qinit/ksw_u8/ksw_i16 in this case). Keep the original SSE2 code untouched under the guard so x86 builds stay identical. Verify by building libfml.a and running the upstream sample (fml-asm test/MT-simu.fq.gz) plus the conan create test_package that actually calls fml_assemble()."
match_keywords: ["emmintrin.h", "x86 and x64 architecture", "SSE2", "__m128i", "aarch64", "scalar fallback", "ksw", "SIMD header", "This header is only meant to be used"]
error_excerpt: "/data/service/hnp/ohos-sdk.org/ohos-sdk_26.0.0.18/ohos/native/llvm/lib/clang/15.0.4/include/emmintrin.h:14:2: error: \"This header is only meant to be used on x86 and x64 architecture\""
severity: P1
category: compat, asm, simd
last_updated: 2026-09-26